      "content": "i get the legal distinction, but that feels like a bit of a technicality. if you look at the actual content of the emails, they all seem to point to the same conclusion that the coordination was intentional. most analysts are saying it's pretty much a clear-cut case of lying to the committee. don't you think the weight of the evidence makes the \"legal weight\" argument a bit of a stretch? like, isn't it basically a fact at this point that they were involved?",
